//=====Tests=====
//Tests are functions that verify that a piece of code is working as expected. They are an essential part of software development and help ensure that code is correct and maintainable. In Rust, tests are defined in a special module called `tests` and are annotated with the `#[test]` attribute. When you run `cargo test`, Rust will compile your code and run all the tests in the `tests` module, reporting any failures or successes. Tests can be used to check the behavior of functions, methods, and even entire modules, making it easier to catch bugs and ensure that your code is working as intended.
